    "title": "Amber Glenn Sets Record at U.S. Figure Skating Championships",
    "text": "•\tAmber Glenn set a record for the women's short program at the U.S. Figure Skating Championships.\n•\tGlenn scored 83.05 points, surpassing Alysa Liu's earlier score of 81.11.\n•\tAlysa Liu is the current world champion.\n•\tIsabeau Levito placed third with 75.72 points.\n•\tThe national championships are the last opportunity for skaters to impress U.S. Figure Skating officials for the Milan Cortina Olympics.\n•\tThe dance competition and men's short program begin Thursday night.\n•\tGlenn's program was set to \"Like A Prayer\" by Madonna.\n•\tAlisa Efimova and Misha Mitrofanov began defense of their U.S. pairs title with a near-perfect short program.\n•\tEfimova and Mitrofanov scored a season-best 75.31 points.\n•\tAudrey Shin and Balazs Nagy placed second in pairs with 67.67 points.\n•\tEllie Kam and Danny O'Shea placed third in pairs with 67.13 points.\n•\tValentina Plazas and Maximiliano Fernandez were within podium reach with 67.03.\n•\tEfimova is waiting for the U.S. to decide whether to waive a three-year waiting period to become a citizen to represent the nation in the Olympics.",
